{
  "type": "doc",
  "content": [
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "content": [
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": "‘Specify only the columns you need.’ Teams sharing a database may have this guideline. Habitual SELECT * retrieves amounts and other fields even when only order status is needed."
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "content": [
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": " "
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "content": [
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": "I used Query Rules to restrict SELECT * against the lab orders table and wrote the message users would see when blocked."
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "content": [
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": " "
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "content": [
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": "I checked the whole sequence: pattern testing, actual DBeaver execution, and audit logs."
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "content": [
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": " "
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "content": [
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": " "
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "heading",
      "attrs": {
        "level": 2
      },
      "content": [
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": "A Status Check Was Retrieving Amounts Too"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "content": [
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": " "
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "content": [
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": "The environment was QueryPie ACP Community 11.6.7 and DBeaver 26.2.4. Demo Developer connected to Orders Control Lab using the same three fictional orders."
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "content": [
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": " "
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "content": [
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": "SELECT * FROM orders_control.orders returned order_id, status, and total_amount. For an order-status check, the first two are enough."
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "content": [
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": " "
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph"
    },
    {
      "type": "image",
      "attrs": {
        "src": "/assets/content/acp-lab-notes/query-rules/01.webp",
        "alt": "Screen 1. Before the rule, SELECT * returns ID, status, and amount.",
        "title": null,
        "width": "100%",
        "height": null,
        "caption": "Screen 1. Before the rule, SELECT * returns ID, status, and amount."
      }
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph"
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "content": [
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": " "
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "content": [
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": "The team rule was simple: explicitly name required columns instead of using an asterisk for this query. This tests SQL-writing guidelines, not a ban on accessing the amount column itself."
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "content": [
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": " "
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "content": [
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": " "
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "heading",
      "attrs": {
        "level": 2
      },
      "content": [
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": "Creating a SQL Rule for the Lab Connection"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "content": [
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": " "
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "content": [
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": "In Databases → Policies → Query Rules, I clicked Create Query Rule, selected Connection, and targeted only Orders Control Lab."
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "content": [
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": " "
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "content": [
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": "Match Type was RegExp and Action was Deny. The pattern detects SELECT * FROM orders_control.orders. Results here are compared for the exact forms tested in this article."
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "content": [
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": " "
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "content": [
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": "I set Error Message to ‘Orders Lab policy: SELECT * is restricted. Please specify the required columns.’ It explains both why the query is blocked and how to fix it."
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "content": [
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": " "
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "content": [
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": " "
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "heading",
      "attrs": {
        "level": 2
      },
      "content": [
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": "Testing Both Queries Before Saving"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "content": [
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": " "
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "content": [
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": "Test Pattern was handy: enter SQL and click Test to immediately check whether it matches."
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "content": [
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": " "
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "content": [
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": "SELECT * FROM orders_control.orders ORDER BY order_id; returned Pattern matched, confirming the intended query was caught."
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "content": [
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": " "
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph"
    },
    {
      "type": "image",
      "attrs": {
        "src": "/assets/content/acp-lab-notes/query-rules/02.webp",
        "alt": "Screen 2. The all-column query matches the pattern. Action and user message are configured on the same screen.",
        "title": null,
        "width": "100%",
        "height": null,
        "caption": "Screen 2. The all-column query matches the pattern. Action and user message are configured on the same screen."
      }
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph"
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "content": [
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": " "
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "content": [
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": "SELECT order_id, status FROM orders_control.orders ORDER BY order_id; returned Pattern not matched. This is not a failed test: it means the query is outside the blocking pattern."
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "content": [
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": " "
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph"
    },
    {
      "type": "image",
      "attrs": {
        "src": "/assets/content/acp-lab-notes/query-rules/03.webp",
        "alt": "Screen 3. Explicitly named columns do not match the blocking pattern.",
        "title": null,
        "width": "100%",
        "height": null,
        "caption": "Screen 3. Explicitly named columns do not match the blocking pattern."
      }
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph"
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "content": [
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": " "
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "content": [
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": "Comparing the blocked and allowed queries in the configuration screen made the intent easy to verify. I then saved."
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "content": [
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": " "
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph"
    },
    {
      "type": "image",
      "attrs": {
        "src": "/assets/content/acp-lab-notes/query-rules/04.webp",
        "alt": "Screen 4. Active rule with priority, target type, pattern, and DENY action.",
        "title": null,
        "width": "100%",
        "height": null,
        "caption": "Screen 4. Active rule with priority, target type, pattern, and DENY action."
      }
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph"
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "content": [
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": " "
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "content": [
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": "I also used the list’s Test function with route PROXY and Orders Control Lab. SQL including DBeaver’s comments still matched, with APPLIED ACTION: DENY."
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "content": [
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": " "
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph"
    },
    {
      "type": "image",
      "attrs": {
        "src": "/assets/content/acp-lab-notes/query-rules/05.webp",
        "alt": "Screen 5. Testing with a specific connection and execution route confirms the rule and DENY result.",
        "title": null,
        "width": "100%",
        "height": null,
        "caption": "Screen 5. Testing with a specific connection and execution route confirms the rule and DENY result."
      }
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph"
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "content": [
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": " "
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "content": [
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": " "
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "heading",
      "attrs": {
        "level": 2
      },
      "content": [
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": "The Custom Guidance Appears in DBeaver"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "content": [
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": " "
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "content": [
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": "After saving, I reopened the DBeaver connection and reran the all-column query. The error area showed my message instead of results."
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "content": [
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": " "
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "content": [
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": "The text ‘SELECT * is restricted. Please specify the required columns.’ was prefixed by query_rule_id: 1, identifying the blocking rule."
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "content": [
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": " "
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph"
    },
    {
      "type": "image",
      "attrs": {
        "src": "/assets/content/acp-lab-notes/query-rules/06.webp",
        "alt": "Screen 6. The all-column query is blocked and the administrator’s message appears in DBeaver.",
        "title": null,
        "width": "100%",
        "height": null,
        "caption": "Screen 6. The all-column query is blocked and the administrator’s message appears in DBeaver."
      }
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph"
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "content": [
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": " "
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "content": [
        {
          "type": "text",
          "marks": [
            {
              "type": "bold"
            }
          ],
          "text": "I liked that the blocked result explained the next step."
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": " Users are told to specify required columns. Operators can explain issues using the same message and rule ID."
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "content": [
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": " "
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "content": [
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": "I named order_id and status and reran the query. Three orders returned successfully with just those two columns."
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "content": [
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": " "
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph"
    },
    {
      "type": "image",
      "attrs": {
        "src": "/assets/content/acp-lab-notes/query-rules/07.webp",
        "alt": "Screen 7. The explicit-column query succeeds, returning only order ID and status.",
        "title": null,
